 "capsule": "Eswatini in this 1969–2025 span covers the final years of British-protectorate Swaziland under King Sobhuza II, independence on 6 September 1968, Sobhuza's 1973 suspension of the Westminster-style constitution to install direct royal rule, and, after his 1982 death and a regency, the long reign of King Mswati III from 1986. In 2018 Mswati III renamed the country from the Kingdom of Swaziland to the Kingdom of Eswatini to mark 50 years of independence, presiding over one of the world's last absolute monarchies amid recurrent pro-democracy protests into the 2020s. This modern sovereign kingdom is distinct from the 19th-century concession-era polity sharing this Wikidata identifier.",
